; The translation tests. OCaml stdlib only, no framework: plain assertions
; that raise on failure and print a pass summary, which is the shape writ's own
; suites use and the shape this code arrived in.
;
; It links the library and the vendored JSON reader — and NOTHING representing
; writ's front end. That absence is the point. Two checks in the original suite
; read the emitted text back through writ's real reader/expander/parser, which
; is the strongest oracle there is for a text generator: asserting on the text
; would pass just as happily if the text were confidently wrong. They cannot
; live here, because vendoring a parser to test against means testing against a
; COPY that ages out of step with the writ anyone actually runs.
;
; They are re-homed in test/pipeline.sh, which runs the real binaries end to
; end. See docs/testing.md.

(test
 (name test_mgtt2writ)
 (deps
  (glob_files fixtures/*.json))
 (libraries mgtt2writ writ_json))
